SUMMARY:🎴 WEEK 7 TUE: Hybrid Azure Mastery Deep Dive (20 cards)
DESCRIPTION:Tuesday - Hybrid & Multi-Pillar Architecture Deep Dive\n\n📚 ANKI DECK:\n→ Hybrid Azure Mastery Deep Dive Batch (20 cards)\n  Topics: 5-pillar integration (Identity→Storage→Compute→Networking→Monitoring), RBAC vs Entra Domain Services identity model, Azure Files double-permission layer (RBAC + NTFS + Kerberos), SMB port 445 hybrid tunneling (VPN/ExpressRoute/SAS tokens), Azure Policy governance vs RBAC, PIM just-in-time privilege elevation, App Service plan scaling architecture, App Service Code vs Docker Container deployment, ACI no-scaling limitation, Bicep vs Terraform IaC performance benchmarks, three-tier VNet subnet design (web/app/db), VNet peering vs VPN gateway, internal load balancer vs Application Gateway, Network Watcher IP Flow Verify and Connection Troubleshoot, Azure Monitor architecture (KQL), metric/log search/activity log alert types, hybrid Azure Monitor Agent deployment, foundational resource tagging + Azure Policy inventory governance\n\n🎧 REFERENCE:\n→ Hybrid Azure Mastery Deep Dive Transcript\n  Full context on how 5 pillars integrate in real operations\n\n⏱️ Schedule:\n- 6-7 AM: Anki Hybrid Mastery (50 cards if available, else 20 core)\n- 7-8 AM: Continue Anki (emphasize mnemonics)\n- 8-9 AM: Break\n- 9-11 AM: Reference transcript; understand pillar dependencies\n- 11-12 PM: Create 5-pillar flowchart (Identity→Storage→Compute→Network→Monitor)\n\n🎯 Goal: Understand how 5 pillars work together; operational dependencies\n💡 Key: Mnemonics from Deep Dive are HIGH-PROBABILITY exam material\n   - 'RBAC opens door; Entra DS decides who touches files'\n   - 'Scale the plan, not the app; engine lifts all cars'\n   - 'ACI Always Create Instance' (no in-place scaling)\n   - 'No tag, no resource' (Azure Policy tagging enforcement)\n\n📌 5-pillar integration = test taker differentiator. Master this.\n\nFinal week of new material! Then comprehensive review.\nLOCATION:Home - Focused Study\CATEGORIES:AZ-104,Week7,Anki,DeepDive,Hybrid,Integration
